    "tol": 0.001,
    "solution": "The matrix is upper triangular, so its determinant is the product of its diagonal entries, $2 \\cdot 8 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 48$. Since $\\det(\\kAinv) = \\frac{1}{\\det(\\kA)}$, the determinant of its inverse is $\\frac{1}{48}$."
   }
