    ],
    "solution": "Both are $3$. Since $S$ is invertible, $\\det(S) \\neq 0$ by Theorem A.6.2, and $\\det(S^{-1}) = \\frac{1}{\\det(S)}$. By Theorem A.6.1, applied twice, $\\det(S^{-1}\\kA S) = \\det(S^{-1})\\det(\\kA)\\det(S) = \\frac{1}{\\det(S)} \\cdot 3 \\cdot \\det(S) = 3$, and in the same way $\\det(S\\kA S^{-1}) = \\det(S)\\det(\\kA)\\det(S^{-1}) = 3$."
